,-0.148835688829422,-8.046303264563903e-05,-2.145764938177308e-06,-4.768370445162873e-07,0.0,-1.1920928244535389e-07,0.0,-5.960462772236497e-07,-0.0003090619284193963,-5.960446742392378e-06,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-7.748573807475623e-06,0.0,-1.1920928244535389e-07,0.0,-1.0728830375228426e-06,-0.0001565095444675535,-0.0012866322649642825,-3.6954811548639555e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,50,3948,400,17,89,488,600,284,22137,488,220,18,2418,220,17399,697,4226,304,279,1352,400,87,488,61697,2418,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nSolve $2z + i = iz + 3.$  Express your answer in the form $x + yi.$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"692cd3dee02718a676bf1d21b0be708e857037f660bd49ecc07e73ff552154f5"},"seconds":24.38952922821045,"seed":556501505776457816,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the equation $2z + i = iz + 3$ for $z$, we follow these steps:\n\nStep 1: Rearrange the equation to group the terms containing $z$ on one side and the constants on the other side.\n\\[\n2z - iz = 3 - i\n\\]\n\nStep 2: Factor out $z$ from the left side of the equation.\n\\[\nz(2 - i) = 3 - i\n\\]\n\nStep 3: Divide both sides of the equation by the coefficient of $z$, which is $(2 - i)$, to solve for $z$.\n\\[\nz = \\frac{3 - i}{2 - i}\n\\]\n\nStep 4: Multiply both the numerator and denominator by the complex conjugate of the denominator to simplify the fraction.\nThe complex conjugate of $2 - i$ is $2 + i$. Therefore,\n\\[\nz = \\frac{(3 - i)(2 + i)}{(2 - i)(2 + i)}\n\\]\n\nStep 5: Simplify the numerator and denominator.\nThe denominator simplifies as follows:\n\\[\n(2 - i)(2 + i) = 4 + 2i - 2i - i^2 = 4 + 1 = 5\n\\]\nThe numerator simplifies as follows:\n\\[\n(3 - i)(2 + i) = 6 + 3i - 2i - i^2 = 6 + i + 1 = 7 + i\n\\]\n\nStep 6: Combine the results to find $z$.\n\\[\nz = \\frac{7 + i}{5} = \\frac{7}{5} + \\frac{1}{5}i\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the solution to the equation in the form $x + yi$ is \\boxed{\\frac{7}{5} + \\frac{1}{5}i}."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{7}{5} + \\frac{1}{5}i}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
